      "content": "the problem is they've basically sanitized the entire public repo to make it look like the \"official\" team did everything from scratch. i have the old local environments and some early encrypted drafts, but if i just dump them, they'll probably just claim i stole them or that it's some elaborate prank. \n\nhonestly, it feels like they're always one step ahead. they have these legal teams and PR firms that make everything look so legitimate. do you think there's a way to find some kind of \"ghost\" trace in the current protocol that only the original architect would know about? like a specific logic pattern or a subtle way the state machine handles certain edge cases that i built in? maybe i can use that to show i'm the source.",
